Fix AOT compatibility warnings in the following core files in `/tmp/sv-4ed2f48a5a27486e87b14285dd3b1f9f/before/`. Make ONLY the specified changes - do not modify anything else.

**1. ArmOperation.cs** - Add `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers]` to the `T` generic parameter in `IsResource<T>()` method.

Current (line 96):
```csharp
private static bool IsResource<T>() where T : notnull
```
Change to:
```csharp
private static bool IsResource<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicConstructors | DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T>() where T : notnull
```
Also add `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` to the using statements if not already present.

**2. GenericOperationSource.cs** - Add `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers]` to the class's `T` type parameter.

Current (line 16):
```csharp
internal class GenericOperationSource<T> : IOperationSource<T>
```
Change to:
```csharp
internal class GenericOperationSource<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicConstructors | DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T> : IOperationSource<T>
```
The file already has `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;`.

**3. ArmClientBuilderExtensions.cs** (in `Extensions/ArmClientBuilderExtensions.cs`) - Add `[RequiresUnreferencedCode]` and `[RequiresDynamicCode]` to the second method `AddArmClient<TBuilder, TConfiguration>`.

Current (lines 27-31):
```csharp
public static IAzureClientBuilder<ArmClient, ArmClientOptions> AddArmClient<TBuilder, TConfiguration>(this TBuilder builder, TConfiguration configuration)
    where TBuilder : IAzureClientFactoryBuilderWithConfiguration<TConfiguration>
{
    return builder.RegisterClientFactory<ArmClient, ArmClientOptions>(configuration);
}
```
Change to:
```csharp
[RequiresUnreferencedCode("Binding strongly typed objects to configuration values is not supported with trimming.")]
[RequiresDynamicCode("Binding strongly typed objects to configuration values requires generating dynamic code at runtime.")]
public static IAzureClientBuilder<ArmClient, ArmClientOptions> AddArmClient<TBuilder, TConfiguration>(this TBuilder builder, TConfiguration configuration)
    where TBuilder : IAzureClientFactoryBuilderWithConfiguration<TConfiguration>
{
    return builder.RegisterClientFactory<ArmClient, ArmClientOptions>(configuration);
}
```
Also add `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` to the using statements.

**4. ArmEnvironment.cs** - Replace `JsonSerializer.Serialize(this)` with manual JSON writing.

Current (line 80):
```csharp
public override string ToString() => JsonSerializer.Serialize(this);
```

Replace with an inline approach that doesn't use JsonSerializer:
```csharp
public override string ToString()
{
    return $"{{\"Endpoint\":\"{Endpoint}\",\"Audience\":\"{Audience}\"}}";
}
```

**5. ArmClientOptions.cs** - Replace `JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>>(span)` with `JsonDocument.Parse`.

Current (lines 51-52):
```csharp
var span = BinaryData.FromStream(stream).ToMemory().Span;
var allProfile = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>>(span);
```

Replace with:
```csharp
var bytes = BinaryData.FromStream(stream);
using var doc = JsonDocument.Parse(bytes);
var allProfile = new Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>();
foreach (var ns in doc.RootElement.EnumerateObject())
{
    var inner = new Dictionary<string, JsonElement>();
    foreach (var item in ns.Value.EnumerateObject())
    {
        inner.Add(item.Name, item.Value.Clone());
    }
    allProfile.Add(ns.Name, inner);
}
```

**6. Four LRO files** - Replace `ToObjectFromJson<Dictionary<string, string>>()` with JsonDocument parsing.

These four files all have the exact same line 61:
- `Resources/Generated/LongRunningOperation/ResourcesArmOperation.cs`
- `Resources/Generated/LongRunningOperation/ResourcesArmOperationOfT.cs`
- `ManagementGroup/Generated/LongRunningOperation/ManagementGroupsArmOperation.cs`
- `ManagementGroup/Generated/LongRunningOperation/ManagementGroupsArmOperationOfT.cs`

Current (line 61):
```csharp
var lroDetails = ModelReaderWriter.Write(rehydrationToken, ModelReaderWriterOptions.Json, AzureResourceManagerContext.Default).ToObjectFromJson<Dictionary<string, string>>();
```

Replace with:
```csharp
using var lroDoc = JsonDocument.Parse(ModelReaderWriter.Write(rehydrationToken, ModelReaderWriterOptions.Json, AzureResourceManagerContext.Default));
var lroDetails = new Dictionary<string, string>();
foreach (var prop in lroDoc.RootElement.EnumerateObject())
{
    lroDetails.Add(prop.Name, prop.Value.GetString());
}
```

For these four files, also add `using System.Text.Json;` to the using statements if not already present.

